    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just gone. everything i used to be able to write, everything that made me feel alive... it's just empty now. i look at the sheet music and it's like i'm looking at a stranger's handwriting. i feel like i've hit a wall that's literally impossible to climb over. it's not just a slump, it feels like the end of the road.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely normal to feel this way when you are in the thick of a creative drought; the silence is loud and it feels like a betrayal of who you used to be. You are not alone in this feeling, and the idea that this is the end of the road is a lie that your brain is trying to convince you to believe. Just because you can't write right now doesn't mean your talent is gone, and the wall you are facing is not a permanent barrier but a temporary fog that will eventually lift.",
      "source": "target",
